---
import { Base, MinisiteNav, PageHero } from '@oimlsmart/site-shell'
import '../styles/app.css'

const NAV = [
  { label: 'About', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Story', href: '/story' },
  { label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' },
  { label: 'Demo', href: '/demo' },
]
---

<Base title="SMART Measuring Instruments" description="OIML SMI — the physical measuring instrument that ships with a standards-defined digital twin.">
  <MinisiteNav sections={NAV} base="/smi" />
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-14">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="OIML SMART · Component 4"
      title="SMART Measuring Instruments"
      lede="A measuring instrument that ships with a standards-defined digital twin: queryable against the Recommendation it was built to, certifiable against it, and surveilled against it for life."
      logo={{ name: 'smi', alt: 'The SMART Measuring Instruments logo.' }}
    />
    <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">The twin is the interface</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">The instrument answers in the Recommendation's own vocabulary: its IS (identity), its HAS (attributes and registers), its DOES (processes and indications). The twin is not a command shell; it is the instrument's model, live.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">A tailored projection</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">The SMART twin is what the Recommendation governs of the instrument's full digital twin: the certified surface. Everything the Recommendation measures and constrains, nothing else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Twin certification</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">A certificate program of its own: the twin's indication is probed against the physical display, and the certificate states the binding holds. The promise is declarative, the evidence is recorded.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Continuous compliance</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">The compliance engine watches the twin against the certified promises: a drift flags, an outage degrades to indeterminate, a re-judgment rides the same verdict chain as the type evaluation.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <p class="mt-10 text-sm"><a href="/smi/docs/" class="text-accent font-medium">Read the SMI documentation →</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
